# `git.status`

Working tree + index status buckets.

**Policy** — read (C0, safe). Capability `ship.git.read`.

## Arguments

None.

## Returns

`StatusBuckets` (JSON).

| field | type |
|-------|------|
| `clean` | `bool` |
| `total` | `number` |
| `staged` | `map` |
| `modified` | `map` |
| `untracked` | `map` |

## Invoke

```
ship ops call git.status --json '{}'
```

Kind: read.

## Example response

```json
{
  "clean": false,
  "total": 3,
  "staged": [
    {
      "path": "crates/core/ship-platform/src/services/checkout.rs",
      "basename": "checkout.rs",
      "status": "A",
      "tone": "added",
      "label": "new file"
    }
  ],
  "modified": [
    {
      "path": "apps/shipd/src/router.rs",
      "basename": "router.rs",
      "status": "M",
      "tone": "modified",
      "label": "modified"
    }
  ],
  "untracked": [
    {
      "path": ".artifacts/checkout-notes.md",
      "basename": "checkout-notes.md",
      "status": "?",
      "tone": "untracked",
      "label": "untracked"
    }
  ]
}
```
